                        "sense_id": "96b119a7-bc0e-3e9a-aab6-f0c661d45f5f",
                        "entry_id": "41ef7f55-7b30-3ad9-b96f-f8d1e80a20ba",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The state of being a peon; the system of paying back debt through servitude and labour; loosely, any system of involuntary servitude."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "56099aa2-a051-47f0-8165-10acf22793b8",
                                "sense_id": "96b119a7-bc0e-3e9a-aab6-f0c661d45f5f",
                                "text": "But there was work to be done down in the Salinas Valley where César Chávez was organizing the grape pickers and lettuce workers out of their state of un-unionized peonage."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e6d5c9ee-67d8-411e-b44f-754a4d9194d2",
                                "sense_id": "96b119a7-bc0e-3e9a-aab6-f0c661d45f5f",
                                "text": "\"It wasn't just the crowds,\" Luis said softly. \"I saw with my own eyes that Díaz's México is a Potemkin village, Miguel. The México profundo where the poor are so hungry they eat grass and bark. I met Indians whose land is being devoured by Díaz's cronies, entire towns swallowed up, and the people reduced to peonage. I talked to Mexican railroad workers who are paid a fraction of what the American owners pay their own countrymen for the same work.\""
                            }
                        ]
                    }
